This project builds on slurm-docker-cluster by Giovanni Torres and
contributors, which provides the containerised Slurm control plane the
benchmark injects faults into.

    https://github.com/giovtorres/slurm-docker-cluster
    Licensed under the MIT License.
    Pinned at commit 978c3ded1f72c1855e528a56559a7a51142eb39c (Slurm 25.11.4).

That project's source is NOT vendored into this repository. `make image`
(cluster/build-image.sh) fetches it at the pinned commit into vendor/, which is
gitignored, refuses to continue if the fetched SHA differs from the pin or the
checkout has local changes, and builds the image from the upstream Dockerfile,
tagged slurmrca/slurm-docker-cluster:25.11.4-978c3de and labelled with the
pinned commit. An existing image with that tag is reused only when its label
names the pinned commit. The compose file under cluster/ is a derived, reduced
configuration written for this benchmark.

All benchmark scenarios, ground truth, harness code, and scoring logic in this
repository are original work.
